"""
Work out where each scraped directory server physically is.

For every ExternalServer row without a country it:
  1. looks the IP up with ip-api.com's batch endpoint (country + city + hosting flag; free tier is
     non-commercial, 100 IPs per request, 15 requests/minute, so the script paces itself),
  2. optionally (--ping) measures round-trip time from THIS machine. From the Singapore primary a low RTT
     is real evidence of "near Singapore" and catches GeoIP rows that are wrong (anycast, VPN, hosting).

Default is a dry run that writes a CSV. --apply writes ExternalServer.country (ISO-2 code) for rows that
have none. Nothing else in the table is touched.

  set -a; . /opt/nxeon/.env; set +a
  python3 /root/nxeon-directory-locate.py --limit 500                 # dry run, CSV only
  python3 /root/nxeon-directory-locate.py --ping --limit 500          # also ping
  python3 /root/nxeon-directory-locate.py --apply                     # write countries

Run --ping from a box you are happy to send ICMP from (see the directory plan: not the primary if you can help it).
"""
